{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <stack>\n#include <utility>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long solve(long long n, int step) {\n    long long a[16];\n    a[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i < 16; ++i)\n        a[i] = a[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n\n    long long ans = 0;\n    stack<pair<long long, int>> st;\n    st.push({n, step});\n    while (!st.empty()) {\n        auto [cur, s] = st.top(); st.pop();\n        long long q = cur / a[s];\n        long long r = cur % a[s];\n        ans += (s + 1LL) * q;\n        if (r == 0) continue;\n        long long option1 = (s + 1LL) + solve(a[s] - r, s - 1);\n        long long option2 = solve(r, s - 1);\n        ans += min(option1, option2);\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    cout << solve(n, 15);\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.util.Stack;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class Pair {\n        long first;\n        int second;\n        Pair(long f, int s) 